[2026-01-30T16:35:11.205Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GMEWqkjnKqnaQaMRq57g9o","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation: Build interactive multi-track timeline with zoom levels, event clustering, and parallel storyline visualization\n     2→\n     3→## Context Area\n     4→Timeline & Flow Visualizations\n     5→\n     6→## Description\n     7→Build interactive multi-track timeline with zoom levels, event clustering, and parallel storyline visualization\n     8→\n     9→## Implementation Details\n    10→\n    11→## Interactive Multi-Track Timeline with Event Clustering\n    12→\n    13→### Vision\n    14→Transform the simple linear timeline into a powerful multi-track visualization that shows parallel storylines, supports semantic zoom from decades to days, clusters dense events intelligently, and enables users to trace how different threads of research interconnect over time.\n    15→\n    16→### Business Value\n    17→- Critical for understanding complex narratives (investigations, market evolution)\n    18→- Reveals patterns invisible in linear timelines\n    19→- Supports comparative analysis across time periods\n    20→- Professional-grade tool for researchers and analysts\n    21→- Differentiates from basic timeline tools\n    22→\n    23→### Scope\n    24→**Included:**\n    25→- Multi-track lanes for different event categories/entities\n    26→- Semantic zoom: decade -> year -> month -> day views\n    27→- Event clustering when too dense to display individually\n    28→- Swimlane layout for parallel storylines\n    29→- Time range selection with brush\n    30→- Compare two time periods side-by-side\n    31→- Event connections showing cause-effect across time\n    32→- Milestone markers for significant events\n    33→- Period annotations (eras, phases)\n    34→- Mini-map for orientation in long timelines\n    35→\n    36→**Out of Scope:**\n    37→- Gantt chart editing capabilities\n    38→- Calendar integration\n    39→\n    40→### Key Components\n    41→1. **MultiTrackTimeline** - Main container with track management\n    42→2. **TimelineTrack** - Individual swimlane for event category\n    43→3. **SemanticZoomController** - Zoom level management\n    44→4. **EventClusterNode** - Collapsed view of dense events\n    45→5. **TimeRangeBrush** - Selection tool for time periods\n    46→6. **CrossTimeConnections** - Lines showing event relationships\n    47→7. **PeriodAnnotations** - Era/phase markers\n    48→8. **TimelineMinimap** - Overview navigation\n    49→9. **ComparePeriods** - Side-by-side time comparison\n    50→\n    51→### Technical Approach\n    52→- D3.js for timeline axis and zooming\n    53→- Temporal clustering algorithm (DBSCAN on time dimension)\n    54→- Canvas rendering for performance with many events\n    55→- Intersection Observer for lazy loading events\n    56→- RequestAnimationFrame for smooth zoom transitions\n    57→- URL state for shareable zoom/position\n    58→\n    59→### Files to Create/Modify\n    60→- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/timeline/MultiTrackTimeline.tsx`\n    61→- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/timeline/TimelineTrack.tsx`\n    62→- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/timeline/SemanticZoomController.tsx`\n    63→- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/timeline/EventClusterNode.tsx`\n    64→- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/timeline/TimeRangeBrush.tsx`\n    65→- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/timeline/CrossTimeConnections.tsx`\n    66→- Create: `src/lib/temporalClustering.ts`\n    67→- Create: `src/hooks/useTimelineZoom.ts`\n    68→- Modify: Timeline.tsx - Upgrade to use new components\n    69→\n    70→### Success Criteria\n    71→- 1000+ events render without lag\n    72→- Zoom from year to day feels smooth\n    73→- Clusters expand on click to show contents\n    74→- Multiple tracks align correctly\n    75→- Time range selection works intuitively\n    76→- Cross-time connections show clearly\n    77→- Minimap reflects current position\n    78→\n    79→### Potential Challenges\n    80→- Performance with many overlapping events\n    81→- Cluster threshold tuning for clarity\n    82→- Cross-track connection routing\n    83→- Responsive layout for narrow viewports\n    84→\n    85→## Instructions\n    86→\n    87→1. Read and understand the implementation details above\n    88→2. Identify all files that need to be modified\n    89→3. Implement the changes following the guidance provided\n    90→4. Ensure code quality and type safety\n    91→5. Test the changes work as expected\n    92→\n    93→## Notes\n    94→\n    95→This requirement was generated from an accepted Development Direction.\n    96→Focus on implementing exactly what is described above.\n    97→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb700aba-f9fc-4283-93cf-561e37220b63","uuid":"f2f75b4a-469a-4e1b-b1a5-88ded79ffe50","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\.claude\\commands\\dir-1769788100098-build-interactive-multi-track-timeline-with.md","content":"# Implementation: Build interactive multi-track timeline with zoom levels, event clustering, and parallel storyline visualization\n\n## Context Area\nTimeline & Flow Visualizations\n\n## Description\nBuild interactive multi-track timeline with zoom levels, event clustering, and parallel storyline visualization\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n## Interactive Multi-Track Timeline with Event Clustering\n\n### Vision\nTransform the simple linear timeline into a powerful multi-track visualization that shows parallel storylines, supports semantic zoom from decades to days, clusters dense events intelligently, and enables users to trace how different threads of research interconnect over time.\n\n### Business Value\n- Critical for understanding complex narratives (investigations, market evolution)\n- Reveals patterns invisible in linear timelines\n- Supports comparative analysis across time periods\n- Professional-grade tool for researchers and analysts\n- Differentiates from basic timeline tools\n\n### Scope\n**Included:**\n- Multi-track lanes for different event categories/entities\n- Semantic zoom: decade -> year -> month -> day views\n- Event clustering when too dense to display individually\n- Swimlane layout for parallel storylines\n- Time range selection with brush\n- Compare two time periods side-by-side\n- Event connections showing cause-effect across time\n- Milestone markers for significant events\n- Period annotations (eras, phases)\n- Mini-map for orientation in long timelines\n\n**Out of Scope:**\n- Gantt chart editing capabilities\n- Calendar integration\n\n### Key Components\n1. **MultiTrackTimeline** - Main container with track management\n2. **TimelineTrack** - Individual swimlane for event category\n3. **SemanticZoomController** - Zoom level management\n4. **EventClusterNode** - Collapsed view of dense events\n5. **TimeRangeBrush** - Selection tool for time periods\n6. **CrossTimeConnections** - Lines showing event relationships\n7. **PeriodAnnotations** - Era/phase markers\n8. **TimelineMinimap** - Overview navigation\n9. **ComparePeriods** - Side-by-side time comparison\n\n### Technical Approach\n- D3.js for timeline axis and zooming\n- Temporal clustering algorithm (DBSCAN on time dimension)\n- Canvas rendering for performance with many events\n- Intersection Observer for lazy loading events\n- RequestAnimationFrame for smooth zoom transitions\n- URL state for shareable zoom/position\n\n### Files to Create/Modify\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/timeline/MultiTrackTimeline.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/timeline/TimelineTrack.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/timeline/SemanticZoomController.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/timeline/EventClusterNode.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/timeline/TimeRangeBrush.tsx`\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/timeline/CrossTimeConnections.tsx`\n- Create: `src/lib/temporalClustering.ts`\n- Create: `src/hooks/useTimelineZoom.ts`\n- Modify: Timeline.tsx - Upgrade to use new components\n\n### Success Criteria\n- 1000+ events render without lag\n- Zoom from year to day feels smooth\n- Clusters expand on click to show contents\n- Multiple tracks align correctly\n- Time range selection works intuitively\n- Cross-time connections show clearly\n- Minimap reflects current position\n\n### Potential Challenges\n- Performance with many overlapping events\n- Cluster threshold tuning for clarity\n- Cross-track connection routing\n- Responsive layout for narrow viewports\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Read and understand the implementation details above\n2. Identify all files that need to be modified\n3. Implement the changes following the guidance provided\n4. Ensure code quality and type safety\n5. Test the changes work as expected\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an accepted Development Direction.\nFocus on implementing exactly what is described above.\n","numLines":97,"startLine":1,"totalLines":97}}}
